<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Pepkor 16 months shr 126 cents.</title>
<headline>Pepkor 16 months shr 126 cents.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sixteen months to June 30, 1996 vs year to Feb 29, 1995</p>
<p>		    (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	    126.0	 vs 110.2</p>
<p>    Div     28.5 making 40	   vs 36</p>
<p>    Net profit	   258.6	 vs 207.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		467.2	 vs 374.5</p>
<p>    Tax		    141.6	 vs 94.5</p>
<p>    Interest paid	121.2	 vs 57.4</p>
<p>    Exceptionals	  10.7 paid  vs received 4.8</p>
<p>    Turnover	  15,931.9	 vs 9,513.6</p>
<p>Div payable Oct 16</p>
<p>on register Sept 13</p>
<p>Full name: Pepkor Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said it had not shared in the retail credit boom, which now seemed to have peaked and it expected improved earnings for the 1997 financial year.</p>
<p>Shareholders will be able to opt for a capitalisation share award instead of the final dividend.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
